From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:10:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 167/170] fix(gastown): file and read warrants in the city
 store the dog pool drains (gcp-1uod)

Warrants poured correctly after gcp-w310 but still never reached a dog. The
dog pool is city-scoped: its demand count and its work query read only the
city store. gc bd answers from a rig store whenever GC_RIG is set or the cwd is
inside a rig, so a warrant filed from a witness session, or from a deacon whose
cwd sat in a rig, landed in the rig store. Every city-store warrant on record
was claimed by a dog; every rig-store warrant (gascity-9qfg, gascity-6w4m,
gcp-zq9r) was never claimed, two of them carrying gc.kind=workflow.

Every producer now defines WARRANT_CITY from GC_CITY_PATH (path-only), falling
back to GC_CITY, and passes --city "$WARRANT_CITY" on its warrant create and
its EXISTING_WARRANT dedupe query: mol-deacon-patrol (3 sites),
mol-witness-patrol and mol-boot-patrol. Each also refuses to file when the city
is unknown, because an empty --city silently falls back to the rig store. The
two reads of the same beads (the deacon's dog work query and the digest's
warrant listing) take the flag too and, writing nothing, no refusal arm.
mol-shutdown-dance's dispatch example and the reason are updated to match.

A rig-aware dog scale_check was ruled out: a dog would spawn, find nothing in
the city store, and drain again.

tests/test_prompt_formula_command_drift.py gains warrant_city_store_violations,
a detector over every create, dedupe and read, and two tests: one proving the
detector catches each rig-store shape, one pinning the real assets at exactly
6 creates, 5 dedupes and 2 reads so a producer reworded out of the detector's
sight fails loudly.

Validation: drift tests green; with --city removed from the boot create the
pin test fails and names mol-boot-patrol.toml. The live drainer probe is the
seat's post-merge data check.
